{
  "source": "course-assets/vector-space/vector-space.mp4",
  "duration": 201.216,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.08,
      "text": "Each AI token starts with a row of numbers called an embedding."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.62,
      "end": 9.78,
      "text": "As the AI processes your message, its layers change those numbers to reflect the surrounding context."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.48,
      "end": 13.76,
      "text": "But those new numbers might not match the starting numbers for any token."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.52,
      "end": 15.9,
      "text": "How can they still represent meaning?"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.28,
      "end": 18.82,
      "text": "An exact match isn't necessary."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.44,
      "end": 21.42,
      "text": "The relationships between the numbers matter too."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.32,
      "end": 28.06,
      "text": "We can picture those relationships as positions on a map, where nearby positions can represent similar meanings."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.06,
      "end": 30.7,
      "text": "That's the idea behind vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.64,
      "end": 34.6,
      "text": "This map uses latitude and longitude to describe position."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.32,
      "end": 40.94,
      "text": "Let's add Dallas with its coordinates 32.78 degrees north, 96.80 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.98,
      "end": 44.62,
      "text": "Next, add Mountain View, then New York City."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.52,
      "end": 48.4,
      "text": "Now you get coordinates that don't match one of our existing cities."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.0,
      "end": 52.42,
      "text": "The first is 38 degrees north, 120 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.98,
      "end": 55.24,
      "text": "Mountain View is closest, even without an exact match."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.24,
      "end": 59.36,
      "text": "Next, try 40 degrees north, 76 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.92,
      "end": 61.62,
      "text": "New York City is closest to the second point."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.46,
      "end": 64.74,
      "text": "The coordinates didn't match either city exactly,"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.74,
      "end": 67.32,
      "text": "but distance helped us find the closest match."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.32,
      "end": 70.54,
      "text": "A map uses two numbers to describe a position,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.9,
      "end": 73.02,
      "text": "but we can do the same with more than two numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.78,
      "end": 75.82,
      "text": "Imagine a taste test where you rate drinks"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.82,
      "end": 76.98,
      "text": "on seven characteristics."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.76,
      "end": 79.44,
      "text": "We can't draw all seven dimensions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.52,
      "end": 82.28,
      "text": "but a simplified picture shows which drinks are closest."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.04,
      "end": 84.24,
      "text": "Let's add Coke to the map."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.24,
      "end": 90.1,
      "text": "Next is Pepsi. Pepsi scores are close to Coke's so it sits near Coke in the soft"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.1,
      "end": 95.18,
      "text": "drinks neighborhood. Now add a hot coffee. Hot coffee scores differ more"
    },
    {
      "start": 95.18,
      "end": 98.72,
      "text": "from Coke's and Pepsi's so it sits farther away in the coffee and tea"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.72,
      "end": 102.58,
      "text": "neighborhood. Now you get numbers that don't match any of our existing"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.58,
      "end": 108.16,
      "text": "drinks. Let's add Mystery Drink A. Mystery Drink A is near Coke and Pepsi."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.54,
      "end": 113.04,
      "text": "Its first six numbers match both. Compare the last number, citrus. Mystery"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.04,
      "end": 119.66,
      "text": "Drink A is 9, Coke is 1, and Pepsi is 10. Pepsi is closest. The citrus gap is only"
    },
    {
      "start": 119.66,
      "end": 125.44,
      "text": "1 compared with 8 for Coke. Now add Mystery Drink B. Mystery Drink B is in"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.44,
      "end": 128.84,
      "text": "the coffee and tea neighborhood. Compare its seven numbers with Hot"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.84,
      "end": 133.02,
      "text": "Coffee's vector. Hot Coffee is closest to Mystery Drink B. Its ratings are"
    },
    {
      "start": 133.02,
      "end": 137.4,
      "text": "similar across all seven dimensions. Each drink's seven numbers give it a"
    },
    {
      "start": 137.4,
      "end": 141.1,
      "text": "position in vector space. Comparing those numbers helps us find the closest"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.1,
      "end": 145.98,
      "text": "This is the idea behind distance. Smaller gaps mean closer positions."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.78,
      "end": 153.42,
      "text": "AI uses this idea on a much larger scale. Its embeddings have thousands of dimensions, with values learned during training."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.08,
      "end": 158.54,
      "text": "After the layers update a token's vector, it doesn't need to match another vector exactly."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.04,
      "end": 161.74,
      "text": "Its position in vector space helps represent its meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.48,
      "end": 166.2,
      "text": "Let's look at this meaning map to see how context changes position."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.2,
      "end": 167.92,
      "text": "Consider the sentence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 168.6,
      "end": 171.32,
      "text": "The tired cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.7,
      "end": 172.8,
      "text": "It soon fell asleep."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.74,
      "end": 176.22,
      "text": "On its own, it could refer to many things."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.0,
      "end": 178.72,
      "text": "As the layers process the sentence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 179.2,
      "end": 183.12,
      "text": "they update its numbers to carry information connecting it to cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.76,
      "end": 186.98,
      "text": "It remains a separate token, now near cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 187.82,
      "end": 191.2,
      "text": "Its new position reflects its connection to cat in this sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.12,
      "end": 194.14,
      "text": "Meaning is a position in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.14,
      "end": 196.9,
      "text": "similar meanings usually sit close together."
    }
  ],
